  "cellsite-burgess-wooley": [
    {
      heading: "Communications Data — Cell Site Analysis",
      paragraphs: [
        "Subject: Martin Burgess. Period requested: 6 January 2022, 14:00–18:00. Requesting officer: Case review team.",
        "Finding: The subject's device connects to a cell sector covering the booked job's street and the adjoining street (Susan Wooley's address falls within the same sector) from 15:14 continuously through to 16:51, at which point it moves to a sector consistent with travel toward Featherton — his next logged appointment. No second booking is recorded at any address within this sector for the period after the first job's expected completion.",
        "Investigative relevance: A routine boiler service of the type logged typically runs 30–45 minutes. The device remains within the same sector for approximately 95 minutes — around 45–50 minutes longer than the booked job alone would account for, with no second job logged to explain the remainder. This is consistent with, and independently corroborates, the subject's own later account (2025 arrest interview) of an unbooked visit of roughly 35 minutes at an adjoining address that afternoon. The sector itself is not narrow enough to confirm presence at any single address — this finding establishes an unexplained gap in his account, not a location.",
        "This is the single most valuable new addition to the Wooley case specifically: the only one of Burgess's three killings with no independent movement-evidence chain until now. Mason has the vehicle/traffic-camera route; Butt has the bus/CCTV/doorbell route; Wooley had nothing beyond Ferris's own unease and the (now-filed) homeowner witness. This closes that gap without over-claiming precision. Cell site data shows which mast/sector a device connected to, not a precise GPS location — it corroborates or complicates an account, it doesn't independently prove presence at an exact address.",
      ],
    },
  ],

